	<sys:String x:Key="MsgNoPhotoFound">No photo found there. Click nearer its middle, or draw a box around it.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="MsgPhotoFound">Photo found and added.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="MsgPhotoRefitted">Box fitted to the photo.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="MsgRefineModeHelp">Refinement mode: draw to crop by hand, Enter to accept, Esc to cancel.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="MsgApplyingRefine">Applying refinement...</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="MsgRefineSuccess">Crop refined successfully.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="MsgRefineCancelled">Refinement cancelled.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="MenuLanguage">Language</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="BtnHelp">Help</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="BtnClose">Close</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HeaderHelp">Controls &amp; Shortcuts</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpSaveResults">There is no Save button: every change is saved to the project as you make it. Moving to the Finish stage writes the crops to Cropped/ as lossless PNGs, and Export in the Finish stage writes the finished photos to Final/.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpSensitivity">How strongly photo edges are looked for. Higher finds fainter borders but may pick up noise. Min/Max photo size and the edge threshold are under the tuning sliders; detection reruns when you stop dragging.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpManualCrop">Drag a rectangle on the scan to add a photo that was not detected. It is added to the list and selected.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpRefine">Draw a tighter crop inside one photo, e.g. to trim a white scanner margin. Accepting re-crops the photo and moves its box on the scan to match (Enter to accept, Esc to cancel).</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpInteractiveBoxesTitle">Editing boxes</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpInteractiveBoxes">Click inside a box to show its photo. Drag a corner to resize it (a magnified view of the spot appears in a corner while you drag, so you can put the edge exactly on the photo's) and the blue handle to rotate it; the photo is re-extracted when you let go. Click the red ✕ on the top-right corner to delete it. Every change can be undone.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpDpiTitle">Scan resolution</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpDpi">The scanner's resolution (e.g. 300 or 600 DPI) is kept in the exported photos, so they print at their real size.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpAutoOrientTitle">AI &amp; Landscape Orientation</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpAutoOrientDesc">Turns photos upright automatically: a face-detection model (YuNet) finds faces, and sky, water and landscape analysis covers photos without people.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpRestoreColorsTitle">Color restoration</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpRestoreColorsDesc">Per photo: presets (faded color print, black &amp; white, sepia, only clean dust, none), an automatic strength, black-and-white/sepia detection and manual brightness, contrast, warmth, tint and saturation. "Copy settings to all" applies one photo's settings to every photo.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpRemoveDustTitle">Dust removal</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpRemoveDustDesc">Finds scanner dust, lint and hairline scratches and fills them in from their surroundings. It can be used on its own, without changing the colors.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpAutoTuneTitle">⚡ Detection Auto-Tune</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpAutoTuneDesc">Tries many combinations of background tolerance, edge threshold and photo size to find difficult or faint photos, without touching the sliders. It can also run on every new scan, or only when little of the scan is covered.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpThemeTitle">Themes &amp; colorblind-friendly boxes</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpThemeDesc">Switch between Dark, Light and System in Settings → Theme. Box Color offers colorblind-friendly presets or any custom color.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpSafeExitTitle">Automatic saving &amp; recovery</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpSafeExitDesc">Scans are written to the project as soon as they arrive, and crop edits and Finish settings are saved as you make them, so closing the app or a crash loses nothing. The last 30 edits can be undone.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpShortcutsTitle">Keyboard Shortcuts</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpShortcutScan">[F5] Scan from flatbed</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpShortcutRotate">[R] Rotate photo 90°</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpShortcutDelete">[Delete] Delete the selected photo(s)</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpShortcutNextScan">[↑ / ↓] Previous / next scan</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpShortcutNextPhoto">[← / →] Previous / next photo</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpShortcutCompare">[Space] Hold to compare with the original crop</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpShortcutSelectAll">[Ctrl+A] Select all photos (Grid)</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpShortcutUndo">[Ctrl+Z] Undo last edit</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpShortcutRedo">[Ctrl+Y] Redo edit</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpShortcutClose">[Esc] Close the dialog, overlay or mode</sys:String>
