	<sys:String x:Key="OptDpi150">150 (Draft / fast)</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="OptDpi300">300 (Standard photos - recommended)</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="OptDpi600">600 (High detail / archival)</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="OptPageAuto">Auto / full bed (detect the maximum)</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="MsgPhotoExported">Exported photo to {0}</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="MsgPhotoExportFailed">Failed to export photo: {0}</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpWorkflowTitle">How it works</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpWorkflowIntro">Each album is a project: a folder chosen or created on the start screen (the project name on the top bar brings it back). A project goes through three stages, shown in the bar at the top. Each one leaves real files in its own folder of the project and never changes the previous one, so you can go back and forth freely.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpStageScanTitle">1 · Scan  →  RawScans/</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpStageScanDesc">Scan pages with your scanner (F5) or import scan files; drag and drop works too. The newest scan is shown large with its photos outlined, so a crooked page can be rescanned at once, or discarded. Every scan is kept unchanged. Double-click a scan to adjust its crops.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpStageCropsTitle">2 · Crops  →  Cropped/</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpStageCropsDesc">Photos are found on each scan automatically. Fix the boxes, add missed photos, rotate and refine them. Crops are saved as lossless PNGs with only geometry fixes: no color changes yet.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpStageFinishTitle">3 · Finish  →  Final/</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpStageFinishDesc">Restore each photo: color, dust, repairs and metadata, with a before/after view. Export writes the finished photos (JPEG or PNG with EXIF) and only redoes those that changed. Photos cropped elsewhere can be imported here directly.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpSectionCrops">Crops stage</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpSectionFinish">Finish stage</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpSectionGeneral">Saving, safety and settings</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpManualCropTitle">Manual crops</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpBackgroundTitle">Background color</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpBackgroundDesc">If photos are missed because the scanner lid or background isn't white, click Pick Color and then the background of the scan. Detection is then auto-tuned for that color; Reset goes back to automatic.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpReviewTitle">Review mode</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpReviewDesc">Go through every photo of every scan full-size to rotate (R) or delete (Delete) them quickly; the wheel or arrow keys move between them. An end slide shows what was done. Esc or a double click goes back to the editor.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpZoom">Use the zoom slider or Ctrl + mouse wheel to zoom into the scan around the pointer, for precise box edits.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpFinishEditorTitle">Photo editor</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpFinishEditorDesc">Click a photo to open it full-window: zoom and pan, drag the before/after split, or hold Space to see the original. The filmstrip and ← / → switch photos; Esc goes back to the grid. Ctrl+click or Shift+click photos in the grid (or tick them) to select several: the bar above the grid applies a preset, turns automatic restoration, dust removal or white-border trimming on or off for all of them (a dash means only some have it), or exports them all in one click. "Trim white border" leaves out a print's white border in the final photo; the preview shades what will be cut. The chips above the grid show one type of photo at a time (black &amp; white, sepia, faded colour, colour); "Suggested by type" gives each selected photo the preset that suits its kind of print. "Adjust" (under Border) lets you drag the trim's edges on the photo; "Automatic" goes back to the border found automatically. ↺ ↻ (or R) turn the photo a quarter turn, for the few that Crops left turned.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpRepairTitle">Repair brush &amp; AI fill</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpRepairDesc">Paint over scratches, creases, tears or stains with the repair brush and they are filled in with grain matched to the photo. For large damage, choose Fill: AI to use the LaMa model (a one-time 208 MB download that runs on your computer). Strokes are kept per photo and can be undone or cleared.</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpSaveTitle">Saving</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpShortcutsCropsTitle">Crops stage</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpShortcutsFinishTitle">Finish photo editor</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpShortcutFinishNav">[← / →] Previous / next photo</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpShortcutFinishCompare">[Space] Hold to see the original</sys:String>
	<sys:String x:Key="HelpShortcutFinishBack">[Esc] Back to the photo grid</sys:String>
